// M5-A3P-1006. Ch19 I03 "The hitch" (E, held input, 4 min, ~140 words): Kerrid's last quiet night.
// act3_ch19.md §2 I03; kerrid.md (Act III: he teaches Rhen the last of what Dace taught him). Night, the plaza's edge.
// Kerrid SITS (he sits since Ch15). He teaches the hitch Dace taught him over eight low tides at the rings: it holds a
// man's weight on a stair and comes free with one pull on the tail. Held inputs: tie, load, pull.
// RULE 5: quiet and practical; he teaches, he doesn't confess; NO FAREWELL is said. Paid in H02 and E3 (§10 Q3).
// RULE 2: nothing names Imra, Dace and Kerrid together (Dace is "your father"; Imra is not mentioned).
title: ch19_the_hitch
location: ch19/iskarra
---
@camera I03
@music kerrid_hitch fade=2.0
@mark kerrid plaza_edge walk
@anim kerrid sit plaza_edge
@mark rhen plaza_edge_b walk
@anim rhen sit plaza_edge_b
@wait 3.0
@anim kerrid hold line_length
Kerrid [neutral]: Give me your hands. #line:ch19_hitch_001
@wait 1.5
Kerrid [neutral]: Your father's. He showed me eight times. I got it on the ninth. #line:ch19_hitch_002
<<event hold_input tie>>
@anim rhen tie_hitch
@wait 3.0
<<event hold_input_end>>
Kerrid [neutral]: Now lean on it. All of you. #line:ch19_hitch_003
<<event hold_input load>>
@anim rhen lean line_length
@wait 3.0
<<event hold_input_end>>
Kerrid [neutral]: Holds anything. Then one pull, and it lets go. #line:ch19_hitch_004
<<event hold_input pull>>
@anim rhen pull line_tail
@sfx rope_slips
@wait 2.0
<<event hold_input_end>>
@wait 3.0
Rhen [neutral]: Why are you teaching me this now? #line:ch19_hitch_005
@wait 2.0
Kerrid [neutral]: Somebody should have it. #line:ch19_hitch_006
<<if $ch17_read_the_ledger>>
    @wait 3.0
    Rhen [sad]: He wrote about the stair. In the ledger. He said the watch captain held the line to the last. #line:ch19_hitch_007
    @wait 3.0
    Kerrid [neutral]: Eight tides. He talked about you every one. #line:ch19_hitch_008
<<endif>>
@wait 4.0
@anim kerrid coil line_length
@wait 3.0
<<set $ch19_learned_the_hitch = true>>
===
